# clang-tidy configuration for sipengine.
#
# The families the project's native audit measured against seeded bugs (bugprone, cert,
# clang-analyzer; ../../../BUILD-STANDARDS.md, "One compiler's warnings are a floor"), plus
# misc, performance and portability. Every finding is an error. What is switched off below is
# switched off for a stated reason, with what would remove the need, which meets this
# project's rule that a suppression must say both.

Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  cert-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  misc-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -misc-use-internal-linkage,
  -performance-enum-size

WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*sipengine.*'
FormatStyle: none

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY EACH IS OFF
#
# bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters
#   The exported C ABI takes (pointer, length) pairs and a total length side by side, the
#   shape every caller of a C buffer API expects, and the internal readers mirror it. The
#   ABI cannot take a struct instead without giving up blittable parameters, which the
#   interop rules in sipengine.h and ../sipnative/README.md require.
#   What would remove this: an ABI of one struct per call, which those rules rule out.
#
# misc-include-cleaner
#   It asks for headers the standard library already guarantees through the ones included,
#   and its answer differs between MSVC's library and libstdc++, so it cannot pass under both.
#   What would remove this: one standard library for every build.
#
# misc-use-internal-linkage
#   Everything internal is already in an anonymous namespace. What is left with external
#   linkage must keep it: the exports sipengine.h declares, the self-test's main, and the
#   fuzzer's entry point, which libFuzzer finds by name.
#   What would remove this: nothing; those three are external by definition.
#
# performance-enum-size
#   It would shrink content::Type to one byte. Its values cross the ABI as uint32_t, are
#   stored in quarantine records as numbers, and must keep their numbers for ever; one width
#   on both sides of the boundary is what keeps that true.
#   What would remove this: nothing; the width is the ABI's.
